<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/"><channel><title>Deck Sanding on eQualle Blog</title><link>https://blog.equalle.com/tags/deck-sanding/</link><description>Recent posts on eQualle Blog</description><generator>Hugo 0.150.1</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:42:46 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.equalle.com/tags/deck-sanding/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>How To Sand Weathered Deck Boards Without Gouging</title><link>https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/10/26/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/10/26/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:42:42 +0000</pubDate><category>Floor &amp; Deck Sanding</category><category>grit-80</category><category>grit-100</category><category>grit-320</category><category>deck sanding</category><category>orbital sander</category><category>grit progression</category><description>Learn how to sand weathered deck boards without gouging. Pro workflow, tool picks, grit choices, and real-world techniques for a smooth, safe deck.</description><summary>&lt;h2 id="deck-sanding-without-gouges-pro-tips-and-steps"&gt;Deck sanding without gouges: pro tips and steps&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Saturday morning, coffee in hand, I ran a palm over the deck rail and felt that familiar sting—another splinter. The boards below were gray and furred like a weathered sweater. Summer chairs wobbled on cupped planks, and the kids tiptoed around the rough spots like they were hot coals. If you’ve been there, you know the feeling: this deck has stories, but it’s due for a reset. That reset starts with deck sanding done right—without carving ruts or dishing out the boards. I’m Lucas Moreno, Workshop &amp;amp; DIY Specialist for eQualle Blog, and I’ve sanded more tired decks than I can count. The good news? You don’t need brute force, a trailer full of machines, or some mystical touch. What you need is a clear plan, a light hand, and the right sequence so your sander never bites harder than it should.&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:content url="https://blog.equalle.com/images/brand/10.webp" medium="image"/><media:content url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/10/26/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding/cards/facebook/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding.jpg" medium="image"/><media:thumbnail url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/10/26/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding/cards/facebook/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/10/26/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding/cards/facebook/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/10/26/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding/cards/instagram/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding.jpg" medium="image"/><media:thumbnail url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/10/26/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding/cards/instagram/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/10/26/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding/cards/instagram/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/10/26/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding/cards/pinterest/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding.jpg" medium="image"/><media:thumbnail url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/10/26/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding/cards/pinterest/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/10/26/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding/cards/pinterest/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/10/26/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding/cards/facebook/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding.jpg" medium="image"/><media:thumbnail url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/10/26/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding/cards/facebook/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/10/26/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding/cards/facebook/how-to-sand-weathered-deck-boards-without-gouging-deck-sanding.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/><readingTime>10</readingTime></item><item><title>Remove Mill Glaze From New Deck Boards By Sanding</title><link>https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/01/14/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/01/14/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Jan 2026 13:45:47 +0000</pubDate><category>Floor &amp; Deck Sanding</category><category>grit-80</category><category>grit-100</category><category>grit-120</category><category>deck sanding</category><category>grit progression</category><category>dust control</category><description>Engineer-tested guide to deck sanding for removing mill glaze on new boards. Tools, grits, workflow, and results for better stain adhesion.</description><summary>&lt;h2 id="deck-sanding-to-remove-mill-glaze-on-new-boards"&gt;Deck sanding to remove mill glaze on new boards&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’ve ever watched fresh rain bead up and roll off a brand-new deck, you’ve seen the surface behave like a waxed car. It looks healthy and waterproof, right up to the moment you try to stain it and the finish flashes unevenly, blotches, or peels in sheets. That isn’t a failure of the stain. It’s the result of mill glaze—an artifact from planing at the mill where knives compress fibers, heat softens lignin, and resins are smeared across the surface, creating a semi-burnished shell. The surest fix is precise, methodical deck sanding. Not a token pass, but a controlled removal of that top layer so finish can mechanically anchor and wick into pores as the manufacturer intended.&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:content url="https://blog.equalle.com/images/brand/17.webp" medium="image"/><media:content url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/01/14/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding/cards/facebook/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding.jpg" medium="image"/><media:thumbnail url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/01/14/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding/cards/facebook/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/01/14/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding/cards/facebook/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/01/14/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding/cards/instagram/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding.jpg" medium="image"/><media:thumbnail url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/01/14/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding/cards/instagram/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/01/14/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding/cards/instagram/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/01/14/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding/cards/pinterest/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding.jpg" medium="image"/><media:thumbnail url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/01/14/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding/cards/pinterest/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/01/14/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding/cards/pinterest/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/01/14/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding/cards/facebook/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding.jpg" medium="image"/><media:thumbnail url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/01/14/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding/cards/facebook/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2026/01/14/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding/cards/facebook/remove-mill-glaze-from-new-deck-boards-by-sanding-deck-sanding.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/><readingTime>9</readingTime></item><item><title>Best Grit For Deck Sanding Before Staining</title><link>https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2025/11/04/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2025/11/04/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 04 Nov 2025 19:32:49 +0000</pubDate><category>Floor &amp; Deck Sanding</category><category>grit-60</category><category>grit-80</category><category>grit-100</category><category>grit-120</category><category>grit-320</category><category>deck sanding</category><category>grit progression</category><description>Engineer-tested guide to the best grit for deck sanding before staining, with abrasive science, tool choices, and proven sanding sequences.</description><summary>&lt;h2 id="best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining"&gt;Best Grit for Deck Sanding Before Staining&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Saturday morning sunlight hits the deck and it looks like two decks at once: the cheerful gathering place you want for the season ahead, and the weathered surface you’ve come to ignore—grayed, patchy stain, a couple of raised splinters in the traffic lane from the back door. If you’ve decided to refresh it, you’ll run into a deceptively technical question right away: what’s the best grit for deck sanding before staining? As a product engineer who field-tests tools and abrasives, I’ve learned that grit choice isn’t a cosmetic preference—it’s a performance variable that decides how well stain bonds, how evenly it soaks, and how long your finish resists UV and foot traffic. In deck sanding, you aren’t polishing furniture; you’re tuning the surface profile to balance penetration and smoothness.&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:content url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2025/11/04/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding/cards/facebook/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding.jpg" medium="image"/><media:thumbnail url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2025/11/04/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding/cards/facebook/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2025/11/04/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding/cards/facebook/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2025/11/04/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding/cards/instagram/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding.jpg" medium="image"/><media:thumbnail url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2025/11/04/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding/cards/instagram/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2025/11/04/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding/cards/instagram/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2025/11/04/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding/cards/pinterest/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding.jpg" medium="image"/><media:thumbnail url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2025/11/04/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding/cards/pinterest/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2025/11/04/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding/cards/pinterest/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2025/11/04/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding/cards/facebook/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding.jpg" medium="image"/><media:thumbnail url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2025/11/04/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding/cards/facebook/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://blog.equalle.com/posts/2025/11/04/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding/cards/facebook/best-grit-for-deck-sanding-before-staining-deck-sanding.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/><readingTime>11</readingTime></item></channel></rss>